A placeholder for the second application, so the shape is visible before there is
anything in it: an application is a folder at the root beside 000_FRAMEWORK, not
a child of a container.

Rename this folder to the application when it exists. Its tables and pages take
a prefix: by default the folder name past the number, spaces removed and
upper-cased (200_XXX is XXX_), or whatever a one-line PREFIX file in the folder
says. The prefix is what travels into SQL, into FW_Pages rows and into error
messages, where a folder cannot follow.

100_CITY NEXUS is the first application and the worked example - its PREFIX file
keeps the CTY_ its tables were created with - and two files decide
what that application is - which tiles its ribbon has, and what occupies its
regions - while everything they call lives in 000_FRAMEWORK.
